If \(n\) is a positive integer, then \(s_{n}\) denotes the sum of all positive integers from 1 to \(n\).

a) For which positive integer \(n\) do we get \(s_{n}=2415\)?

b) For which positive integer \(m\) is \(s_{m}\) exactly 69 times as large as \(m\)?

\section*{a) It holds that \(s_{n}=\frac{n(n+1)}{2}\).}

